{
  "email": "hannah.lee@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports temporary password rejected and password change fails with error after 3 attempts. Checking account status and must_change_password per KB-003."
}

{
  "user_id": 12,
  "reason": "Checking recent sign-in attempts for the password change failures (network, result, location) per KB-003 quick checks."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, I checked your account. It's active and not locked, and it's set to require a new password at your next sign-in, so your temporary password was accepted. The problem is likely in how the change is being submitted. Please try these steps: 1) Use your work laptop's Windows sign-in screen (not a web page), and connect to the office network or VPN first. 2) Turn off Caps Lock and check that your keyboard is set to English, and watch for l vs I and 0 vs O. 3) Make sure the new password is at least 14 characters and different from any recent password. If it still shows an error, reply with the exact wording of the message and the time you tried, and we'll look into it further.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user: active, not blocked, failed_login_count 0, must_change_password true, password_last_set 2026-10-11, VPN enabled, usual hours 09:00-17:00 New York. Checked sign-in logs: 10 entries, all successful, corporate or residential networks, New York only, no failed_password results and no hosting-network sign-ins. The logs show nothing from the attempted password changes, which suggests the change request may be failing before it reaches authentication, possibly on the web change-password page. No lockout, so unlock is not needed. KB-003 escalation condition (active with no change required) does not apply because must_change_password is true. Did not run reset_password (not needed, and the temp password is still valid per the account). Next steps: have user retry on the laptop sign-in screen per KB-003. If it still fails with the same error, escalate to Tier 2 with the exact error text and the timestamps, and check whether the change-password path is blocked by a policy. Consider reissuing a temp password via KB-002 only if the user confirms the temp password itself is rejected.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-003",
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
